# Unreal generated output. Only Config, project descriptor and selected Content
# are committed under UnrealPort.
/UnrealPort/Binaries/
/UnrealPort/DerivedDataCache/
/UnrealPort/Intermediate/
/UnrealPort/Saved/
/UnrealPort/.vs/
/UnrealPort/Build/

# Marketplace packs downloaded for evaluation. Excluded because three of their
# files break GitHub's hard 100 MB per-file limit (T_Backpack_Normal 150 MB,
# Example_Stationary_2_BuiltData 123 MB, T_Jacket_Normal 118 MB) -- committing
# any of them makes the branch unpushable, not merely heavy. They are one-click
# re-downloadable from the Epic launcher, so nothing unrecoverable is lost.
# If a character or prop from one of these is chosen for the game, un-ignore
# that specific pack (and shrink the oversized files) so a clone still builds.
/UnrealPort/Content/AE_BR_Props/
/UnrealPort/Content/ModSciInteriors/
/UnrealPort/Content/ModSci_EngiProps/
/UnrealPort/Content/ModSci_Engineer/
/UnrealPort/Content/QuantumCharacter/
/UnrealPort/Content/Survival_Character/
/UnrealPort/Content/__ExternalActors__/QuantumCharacter/
/UnrealPort/Content/__ExternalActors__/Survival_01/
/UnrealPort/Content/__ExternalActors__/Survival_Character/
/UnrealPort/Content/__ExternalObjects__/QuantumCharacter/
/UnrealPort/Content/__ExternalObjects__/Survival_Character/

# Character packs pulled from the launcher vault purely to be looked at and
# bone-checked. Same rule as above: whichever character is actually chosen for
# the game gets un-ignored so a clone still builds.
